GARDEN FREE USE / PUBLIC RELEASE AND FUTURE GOVERNANCE NOTICE

Effective public-release date: 2026-10-06
Governance clarification: 2026-10-07

CURRENT STATUS — FREE FOR EVERYONE

The Garden project owner has made Garden free for everyone.

Anyone may use the rights granted by this license under the terms below. The owner believes Garden ideas may have very large economic value—potentially billions or trillions if their claimed usefulness proves out—but has nevertheless chosen the fully-free option as the current state.

IF ANYONE WANTS TO CHANGE THE FREE STATUS

There are only two intended economic-governance outcomes:

OPTION 1 — FULLY FREE FOR EVERYONE

This is the current state.

OPTION 2 — GARDEN COMMON FUND

If Garden is ever moved away from the fully-free model, then, to the extent Garden-related economic rights, future material, assets, proceeds, or other interests remain legally controllable, they are intended to be held by a Garden Common Fund rather than placed under private or political control.

Spending and economic-governance decisions would be made democratically by approximately 100,000 randomly selected, periodically rotating ordinary people through a mechanism designed to be politically independent and strongly resistant to corruption, coercion, government interference, corporate capture, concentrated wealth, organized capture and permanent control.

Those voters would be temporary governors, not shareholders. Voting authority would not create transferable, saleable or inheritable personal ownership shares. The Garden Common Fund would hold the relevant common assets and the selected community would decide spending.

The exact selection, identity, voting, audit, rotation and anti-capture mechanisms can be designed and tested if this second option ever needs to be activated.

NO THIRD OPTION IS INTENDED

A move away from free use is not intended to create permanent government, political-party, corporate, billionaire, administrator or other privileged private control.

EXISTING GRANTS ARE NOT RETROACTIVELY CANCELLED

The public release below granted some permissions expressly on a perpetual or irrevocable basis. This governance clarification does not claim to retroactively cancel rights already validly granted under the 2026-10-06 release. The Common Fund alternative therefore concerns rights, future material, assets, proceeds or interests that remain controllable.

